-- allium: 3
-- quota.allium — storage quotas: rules, groups, who they govern, and which storage-consuming operations they refuse.
--
-- Feature switch: [quota] ENABLED (config.enabled, default off) removes every
--   quota surface (admin API, user/org usage API and storage overview pages:
--   their exposures are guarded by it) and admits every storage-growing
--   operation; every management rule below requires it. Login-source sync of
--   quota groups is not switched: Forgejo records memberships either way.
-- Scope: Instance-wide storage quota for users and organizations ("quota holders"),
--   in bytes (size:* subjects) and, since follow-up 2, in numbers of things
--   owned (count:* subjects: repositories, packages, package versions).
--   An administrator defines quota rules (a byte limit over a set of storage
--   subjects), bundles them into quota groups, and assigns holders to groups
--   (explicitly, via configured default groups, or via OAuth2 group claims at
--   sign-in). Before any operation that would grow a holder's storage, the
--   holder's current usage is evaluated against their effective groups and the
--   operation is refused when the holder is over quota for that subject (or
--   would be, counting the incoming size, where that size is known up front).
-- Includes:
--   QuotaSubject hierarchy, QuotaRule, QuotaGroup, QuotaGroupRule (group<->rule
--   link), QuotaAccount (the quota view of a user or organization),
--   QuotaGroupMembership, QuotaUsage (measured storage), the evaluation
--   algorithm, the enforcement table (which operation checks which subject and
--   charges whom), admin management (API), holder self-service usage
--   reporting (web storage overview + API), OAuth2 group-claim sync into
--   quota groups.
-- Excludes:
--   - (decided, packages 6: the former [packages] LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_* and
--     LIMIT_SIZE_<KIND> limits are gone; package storage is limited only by
--     quota rules on size:assets:packages:all, see config.default_packages.
--     decided, follow-up 2: LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_COUNT comes back as a default
--     count rule on count:packages:versions, see config.default_package_versions.)
--   - How each storage figure is measured on disk (git object size, LFS size,
--     blob dedup): the measuring belongs to code/packages/actions; quota only
--     consumes the figures (see QuotaUsage).
--   - The 413 response format / HTML "Quota exceeded" page: transport detail.
--   - The legacy `Rule.Acceptable` (<=) helper: unused by any caller.
-- Emits:
--   StorageConsumptionAdmitted(account, subject, operation)
--       -- the quota gate let a storage-growing operation through.
--   QuotaGroupsChanged(account)
--       -- a holder's explicit group set changed (admin or login sync).
-- Reacts to:
--   StorageConsumptionRequested(requester, account, subject, operation, incoming)
--       -- the gate contract (surface QuotaGateReference). Gated operations in
--          repositories, code, releases, issues, wiki, pulls, packages and
--          actions honour it as `requires: quota_allows(<charged>, <subject>,
--          <incoming bytes or null>)` in their own rules; nothing emits it as a
--          trigger.
--   accounts/UserAccountCreated(user)
--       -- the new account's QuotaAccount is created.
--   authentication/ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)
--       -- authentication's sign-in / registration / account link through an
--          external source (OAuth2 or LDAP); the source's quota group mapping
--          applies.

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./authentication.allium" as authentication
use "./access.allium" as access

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- (none: users, organizations and login sources are imported)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a holder currently uses, in bytes. Every figure is charged to the
-- OWNER of the thing, never to whoever uploaded it: attachments, artifacts and
-- LFS objects in a repository count against the repository's owner; packages
-- count against the package owner.
-- decided (quota 3): wiki storage is measured, as size:wiki, and counts under
-- size:git:all (it is git data), no longer under size:assets:all.
-- from: models/quota/used.go:17
value QuotaUsage {
    -- git size of the holder's public repositories
    repos_public: Integer
    -- git size of the holder's private repositories
    repos_private: Integer
    -- LFS size of all the holder's repositories
    git_lfs: Integer
    -- attachments on issues/PRs/comments in the holder's repositories
    attachments_issues: Integer
    -- attachments on releases in the holder's repositories
    attachments_releases: Integer
    -- compressed size of live (not expired / pending deletion / deleted)
    -- Actions artifacts in the holder's repositories
    artifacts: Integer
    -- distinct package blobs referenced by packages the holder owns (directly
    -- or via a repository the holder owns); a blob shared by many versions
    -- counts once
    packages: Integer
    -- git size of the wikis of all the holder's repositories (measured by
    -- wiki; Forgejo reported 0)
    wiki: Integer
    -- decided (follow-up 2): counts, for the count:* subjects. Not bytes, and
    -- never part of `all`.
    -- repositories the holder owns (repositories/Repository.owner)
    repos_count: Integer
    -- non-internal packages the holder's registry holds
    packages_count: Integer
    -- non-internal package versions the holder's registry holds (what
    -- Forgejo's LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_COUNT counted)
    -- from: services/packages/packages.go:395
    package_versions_count: Integer

    repos_all: repos_public + repos_private
    git_all: repos_all + git_lfs + wiki
    attachments_all: attachments_issues + attachments_releases
    assets_all: attachments_all + artifacts + packages
    all: git_all + assets_all
}

-- One line of the enforcement table: which subject an operation is checked
-- against and whose quota is charged.
-- from: routers/api/v1/api.go:761
value QuotaGate {
    operation: QuotaGatedOperation
    subject: QuotaSubject
    charged: ChargedParty
}

-- One entry of a "create group with rules" request.
-- from: modules/structs/quota.go:91
value QuotaRuleSpec {
    name: String
    limit: Integer?
    subjects: Set<QuotaSubject>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Storage subjects. Wire names in comments. They form a tree; a rule that
-- names a subject also governs every descendant of it:
--
--   size:all                                   all
--   ├─ size:git:all                            git_all
--   │  ├─ size:git:lfs                         git_lfs
--   │  ├─ size:repos:all                       repos_all
--   │  │  ├─ size:repos:public                 repos_public
--   │  │  └─ size:repos:private                repos_private
--   │  └─ size:wiki                            wiki
--   └─ size:assets:all                         assets_all
--      ├─ size:assets:attachments:all          attachments_all
--      │  ├─ size:assets:attachments:issues    attachments_issues
--      │  └─ size:assets:attachments:releases  attachments_releases
--      ├─ size:assets:artifacts                artifacts
--      └─ size:assets:packages:all             packages
--
-- decided (quota 3): size:wiki sits under size:git:all (Forgejo listed it
-- under size:assets:all and never measured it).
--
-- Count subjects stand beside the tree, each on its own (no ancestor, no
-- descendant): a rule on one limits how many of those things a holder owns,
-- and an operation that adds one asks with incoming = 1.
--
--   count:repos                                repos_count
--   count:packages                             packages_count
--   count:packages:versions                    package_versions_count
--
-- decided (follow-up 2): quota gains count subjects next to the byte
-- subjects (Forgejo had byte subjects only; package counts were a separate
-- [packages] setting).
-- from: models/quota/limit_subject.go:13
enum QuotaSubject {
    size_all
    | size_repos_all | size_repos_public | size_repos_private
    | size_git_all | size_git_lfs
    | size_assets_all
    | size_assets_attachments_all | size_assets_attachments_issues | size_assets_attachments_releases
    | size_assets_artifacts | size_assets_packages_all
    | size_wiki
    | count_repos | count_packages | count_package_versions
}

-- Every operation that consults the quota gate before it runs.
-- from: services/context/quota.go:110
enum QuotaGatedOperation {
    create_repository | generate_repository_from_template | fork_repository
    | migrate_repository | retry_migration
    | transfer_repository | accept_repository_transfer
    | git_push | lfs_upload
    | edit_files | upload_files | apply_diff_patch | cherry_pick
    | create_branch | create_tag
    | create_release | edit_release | upload_release_attachment
    | upload_issue_attachment
    | edit_wiki_page
    | merge_pull_request | update_pull_request_branch | apply_review_suggestion
    | sync_mirror_manually | sync_mirror_scheduled
    | upload_package | upload_actions_artifact
    | create_package | create_package_version
}

-- Whose quota an operation is charged to.
enum ChargedParty {
    repository_owner          -- owner of the repository being written to
    target_owner              -- the user/org that will own the new repository
    transfer_recipient        -- the user/org receiving the repository
    head_repository_owner     -- owner of a PR's head (fork) repository
    package_owner             -- owner of the package (uploader when none yet)
}

enum MembershipOrigin {
    admin_assigned | login_source_sync
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A limit over a set of subjects: bytes for size:* subjects, a number of
-- things for a count:* subject. A rule names either size subjects only or
-- exactly one count subject (decided: follow-up 2; units never mix). The limit applies to the usage of the
-- UNION of the listed subjects: each byte counts once per rule, so a rule on
-- {size:all, size:git:all} measures exactly size:all.
-- decided (quota 4): union, not a sum (Forgejo summed overlapping subjects twice).
-- decided (quota 2): the incoming size is counted where it is known up front.
-- from: models/quota/rule.go:13
entity QuotaRule {
    name: String                      -- unique, immutable identity
    limit: Integer                    -- bytes (or things, for a count subject); -1 means unlimited; 0 forbids any growth
    subjects: Set<QuotaSubject>

    group_links: QuotaGroupRule with rule = this

    is_unlimited: limit = -1

    -- The rule governs `subject` when it names the subject or any ancestor of it.
    covers(s): subjects.any(x => x in subject_lineage(s))

    -- With a known incoming size: usage + incoming <= limit. With no size known
    -- up front (a push, checked on receipt): strictly below the limit, so a
    -- holder exactly AT the limit is over quota.
    permits(u, incoming): limit = -1
        or (incoming = null and usage_union(u, subjects) < limit)
        or (incoming != null and usage_union(u, subjects) + incoming <= limit)
}

-- A named bundle of rules.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:16
entity QuotaGroup {
    name: String                      -- unique, immutable identity

    rule_links: QuotaGroupRule with group = this
    memberships: QuotaGroupMembership with group = this

    -- The group has an opinion on `s` when any of its rules covers it.
    matches(s): rule_links.any(l => l.rule.covers(s))

    -- Every covering rule must permit; the first covering rule that does not
    -- permit decides "deny" for this group.
    permits(s, u, incoming): rule_links.all(l => not l.rule.covers(s) or l.rule.permits(u, incoming))
}

-- A rule belongs to any number of groups.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:25
entity QuotaGroupRule {
    group: QuotaGroup
    rule: QuotaRule
}

-- The quota view of one user or organization. Exists implicitly for every
-- holder; exactly one of user / organization is set.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:37
entity QuotaAccount {
    user: accounts/User?
    organization: organizations/Organization?

    -- measured by the owning modules (see QuotaUsage)
    usage: QuotaUsage

    memberships: QuotaGroupMembership with account = this
    has_explicit_groups: memberships.count > 0
}

-- Assignment of a holder to a group.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:37
entity QuotaGroupMembership {
    group: QuotaGroup
    account: QuotaAccount
    origin: MembershipOrigin
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [quota] ENABLED: when false nothing is gated, and every quota API/web
    -- page (admin, user, org) is absent.
    enabled: Boolean = false
    -- [quota] DEFAULT_GROUPS: names of groups governing every holder that has
    -- no explicit group. Names that do not exist are ignored.
    default_groups: Set<String> = {}
    -- decided (follow-up 2): [packages] LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_COUNT restored as
    -- a third built-in fallback rule, on count:packages:versions: how many
    -- non-internal package versions a holder without groups may own. -1 =
    -- unlimited (Forgejo's default). Holders with explicit or default groups
    -- get count limits from rules on count:* subjects in those groups. There
    -- is no built-in count:repos rule: repositories' per-owner creation limit
    -- (MAX_CREATION_LIMIT / max_repo_creation) already plays that part.
    -- from: modules/setting/packages.go:49
    default_package_versions: Integer = -1
    -- [quota.default] TOTAL: limit of the built-in fallback rule (subject
    -- size:all) used when a holder has neither explicit nor default groups.
    -- -1 = unlimited. Accepts byte-size notation ("1 GiB").
    default_total: Integer = -1
    -- decided (packages 6): package limits are default quota rules. Limit of
    -- a second built-in fallback rule (subject size:assets:packages:all) in
    -- the same fallback group; replaces [packages] LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_SIZE.
    -- -1 = unlimited. Holders with explicit or default groups get package
    -- limits from rules on size:assets:packages:all in those groups.
    default_packages: Integer = -1
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The enforcement table. A rebuild must consult the gate at each of these
-- points; the subject and the charged party are part of the contract.
-- from: routers/api/v1/api.go:761 / routers/web/web.go:1480 / routers/private/hook_pre_receive.go:184

default QuotaGate gate_create_repository = { operation: create_repository, subject: size_repos_all, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_generate_repository = { operation: generate_repository_from_template, subject: size_repos_all, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_fork_repository = { operation: fork_repository, subject: size_repos_all, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_migrate_repository = { operation: migrate_repository, subject: size_repos_all, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_retry_migration = { operation: retry_migration, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
-- decided (quota 5): a transfer charges the new owner (user or organisation) on every path,
-- web and API, request and acceptance alike (Forgejo's web accept charged the accepting user)
default QuotaGate gate_transfer_repository = { operation: transfer_repository, subject: size_repos_all, charged: transfer_recipient }
default QuotaGate gate_accept_transfer = { operation: accept_repository_transfer, subject: size_repos_all, charged: transfer_recipient }
default QuotaGate gate_git_push = { operation: git_push, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_lfs_upload = { operation: lfs_upload, subject: size_git_lfs, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_edit_files = { operation: edit_files, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_upload_files = { operation: upload_files, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_apply_diff_patch = { operation: apply_diff_patch, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_cherry_pick = { operation: cherry_pick, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_create_branch = { operation: create_branch, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_create_tag = { operation: create_tag, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_create_release = { operation: create_release, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_edit_release = { operation: edit_release, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_release_attachment = { operation: upload_release_attachment, subject: size_assets_attachments_releases, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_issue_attachment = { operation: upload_issue_attachment, subject: size_assets_attachments_issues, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_wiki = { operation: edit_wiki_page, subject: size_wiki, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_merge_pull = { operation: merge_pull_request, subject: size_git_all, charged: repository_owner }
-- decided: requests 3 — "update branch" charges the head repository's owner,
-- where the commits land (as an applied suggestion does)
default QuotaGate gate_update_pull = { operation: update_pull_request_branch, subject: size_git_all, charged: head_repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_apply_suggestion = { operation: apply_review_suggestion, subject: size_git_all, charged: head_repository_owner }
-- decided (quota 6): a manual mirror sync is gated on size:git:all, like a push, on web and API
default QuotaGate gate_mirror_manual = { operation: sync_mirror_manually, subject: size_git_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_mirror_scheduled = { operation: sync_mirror_scheduled, subject: size_repos_all, charged: repository_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_package_upload = { operation: upload_package, subject: size_assets_packages_all, charged: package_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_artifact_upload = { operation: upload_actions_artifact, subject: size_assets_artifacts, charged: repository_owner }

-- Count gates (decided: follow-up 2). Each is asked with incoming = 1, beside
-- the size gate of the same operation where it has one. A new repository
-- counts against the owner it will have; a repository's arrival by transfer
-- counts against the recipient. repositories folds the count:repos check into
-- its per-owner creation limit (within_creation_limit), so the instance
-- MAX_CREATION_LIMIT / per-user max_repo_creation and quota count rules are
-- one check there, and both must allow.
default QuotaGate gate_create_repository_count = { operation: create_repository, subject: count_repos, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_generate_repository_count = { operation: generate_repository_from_template, subject: count_repos, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_fork_repository_count = { operation: fork_repository, subject: count_repos, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_migrate_repository_count = { operation: migrate_repository, subject: count_repos, charged: target_owner }
default QuotaGate gate_transfer_repository_count = { operation: transfer_repository, subject: count_repos, charged: transfer_recipient }
default QuotaGate gate_accept_transfer_count = { operation: accept_repository_transfer, subject: count_repos, charged: transfer_recipient }
-- the first upload under a new package name (or first manifest of a new image)
default QuotaGate gate_create_package = { operation: create_package, subject: count_packages, charged: package_owner }
-- every upload or manifest push that adds a version (re-pointing a container
-- tag replaces one and is not counted)
-- from: services/packages/packages.go:226
default QuotaGate gate_create_package_version = { operation: create_package_version, subject: count_package_versions, charged: package_owner }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- ---- The gate ----------------------------------------------------------

-- The single decision every gated operation defers to. Where the operation
-- knows its size up front (web file edits and uploads, LFS objects, wiki
-- pages, attachments, packages, artifacts) `incoming` carries it and the check
-- is usage + incoming <= limit; where it does not (a git push, checked on
-- receipt; repository creation, migration, transfer) `incoming` is null and
-- the check is current usage strictly below the limit.
--
-- quota_allows(account, subject, incoming), precisely:
--   0. when config.enabled is false: always true (nothing is gated).
--   1. groups := account's explicit groups; if none, the existing groups
--      named in config.default_groups; if still none, a built-in group with
--      the rules { limit: config.default_total, subjects: {size_all} },
--      { limit: config.default_packages, subjects: {size_assets_packages_all} }
--      (both must permit a package upload) and
--      { limit: config.default_package_versions, subjects: {count_package_versions} }
--      (decided: follow-up 2, the former LIMIT_TOTAL_OWNER_COUNT).
--   For a count subject `incoming` is 1 (one more repository, package or
--   version) and the usage is the matching count in QuotaUsage, so a holder
--   may own exactly `limit` of them.
--   2. if NO group in groups matches(subject): allowed.
--   3. otherwise allowed iff SOME group in groups both matches(subject) and
--      permits(subject, account.usage, incoming).
--   Consequence: only a rule that covers a subject can deny it, and one
--   permissive group overrides any number of restrictive ones.
-- from: models/quota/quota.go:20
-- decided (quota 1): a subject no rule covers is allowed (Forgejo denied it).
-- decided (quota 2): the incoming size is counted wherever it is known up front.
-- decided (quota 7): an operation that can only shrink storage (deleting
-- files through the API or web editor, deleting refs, pages, attachments,
-- packages) never asks the gate, so quota never refuses it.
-- decided (packages 6): the built-in fallback group also carries the default
-- package rule (config.default_packages); packages has no limits of its own
-- decided (follow-up 2): count subjects are gated through the same decision,
-- with incoming = 1; the built-in group's count rule is config.default_package_versions
rule StorageConsumptionGated {
    when: StorageConsumptionRequested(requester, account, subject, operation, incoming)
    requires: not config.enabled or quota_allows(account, subject, incoming)
    ensures: StorageConsumptionAdmitted(account: account, subject: subject, operation: operation)
    @guidance
        -- Enforcement points (web, API, git, LFS, package registry, Actions
        -- artifact endpoint) are listed as QuotaGate defaults. Notable details:
        -- * git push (pre-receive): only ref updates that are not deletions are
        --   refused; deleting branches/tags is always allowed so a holder can
        --   free space. AGit refs (refs/for/*) and refs/pull/* are not gated.
        --   Pushes to PROTECTED branches are exempt while
        --   code/config.quota_exempts_protected_branches is true (the default,
        --   Forgejo's behaviour); an admin who sets it false gets them checked
        --   like every other push (decided under code 1, quota 9).
        -- * file changes through the web editor or API: a change set that only
        --   deletes files is not gated (decided, quota 7).
        -- * manual mirror sync (web and API): size:git:all (decided, quota 6).
        -- * LFS: the batch "upload" operation and the object PUT are gated only
        --   when the object is not already stored.
        -- * scheduled pull-mirror sync is silently skipped (not failed) while
        --   the owner is over quota; a manual sync reports an error.
        -- * package upload is charged to the package owner, so members
        --   uploading into an organization consume the organization's quota.
        -- * apply-suggestion is charged to the PR head repository owner.
}

-- ---- Quota accounts ----------------------------------------------------

-- Every new account gets its quota view at once (every account-creation path
-- in accounts emits UserAccountCreated), so the gate and a first sign-in's
-- group sync (LoginSourceSyncsQuotaGroups) find it. Organisations' quota
-- accounts are implicit (see QuotaAccount).
rule CreateQuotaAccountForNewUser {
    when: accounts/UserAccountCreated(user)
    requires: not exists QuotaAccount{user: user}
    ensures: QuotaAccount.created(user: user, organization: null)
}

-- ---- Rule management (site admin) ------------------------------------

-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/quota_rule.go:78
rule AdminCreatesQuotaRule {
    when: AdminCreatesQuotaRule(admin, name, limit, subjects)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: name != ""
    requires: limit != null
    requires: limit >= -1
    -- decided (follow-up 2): size subjects only, or exactly one count subject
    requires: subjects.count = 1 or subjects.all(x => x not in {count_repos, count_packages, count_package_versions})
    requires: not exists QuotaRule{name: name}
    ensures: QuotaRule.created(name: name, limit: limit, subjects: subjects)
}

-- Name is immutable; only limit and/or subjects change. Unknown subject names
-- are refused before anything changes.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/quota_rule.go:150
rule AdminEditsQuotaRule {
    when: AdminEditsQuotaRule(admin, rule, new_limit, new_subjects)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: new_limit = null or new_limit >= -1
    -- decided (follow-up 2): an edit may not mix count and size subjects
    requires: new_subjects = null or new_subjects.count = 1 or new_subjects.all(x => x not in {count_repos, count_packages, count_package_versions})
    ensures:
        if new_limit != null:
            rule.limit = new_limit
        if new_subjects != null:
            rule.subjects = new_subjects
}

-- Deleting a rule detaches it from every group.
-- from: models/quota/rule.go:142
rule AdminDeletesQuotaRule {
    when: AdminDeletesQuotaRule(admin, rule)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    let links = rule.group_links
    ensures:
        for l in links:
            not exists l
    ensures: not exists rule
}

-- ---- Group management (site admin) -----------------------------------

-- Creates the group and, atomically, its rules: a spec naming an EXISTING
-- rule attaches that rule as it is (the spec's limit/subjects are ignored); a
-- spec naming a new rule creates it (missing limit = 0). Any failure (duplicate
-- group name, unknown subject) creates nothing.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/quota_group.go:33
rule AdminCreatesQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminCreatesQuotaGroup(admin, name, rule_specs)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: name != ""
    requires: not exists QuotaGroup{name: name}
    -- decided (follow-up 2): no new rule may mix count and size subjects
    requires: rule_specs.all(spec => spec.subjects.count = 1 or spec.subjects.all(x => x not in {count_repos, count_packages, count_package_versions}))
    ensures:
        let group = QuotaGroup.created(name: name)
        for spec in rule_specs:
            if exists QuotaRule{name: spec.name}:
                QuotaGroupRule.created(group: group, rule: QuotaRule{name: spec.name})
            else:
                let fresh = QuotaRule.created(name: spec.name, limit: spec.limit ?? 0, subjects: spec.subjects)
                QuotaGroupRule.created(group: group, rule: fresh)
}

-- Deleting a group removes its rule links and memberships; the rules survive.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:276
rule AdminDeletesQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminDeletesQuotaGroup(admin, group)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    let links = group.rule_links
    let members = group.memberships
    ensures:
        for l in links:
            not exists l
    ensures:
        for m in members:
            not exists m
            QuotaGroupsChanged(account: m.account)
    ensures: not exists group
}

-- from: models/quota/group.go:126
rule AdminAddsRuleToQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminAddsRuleToQuotaGroup(admin, group, rule)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: not exists QuotaGroupRule{group: group, rule: rule}
    ensures: QuotaGroupRule.created(group: group, rule: rule)
}

-- from: models/quota/group.go:157
rule AdminRemovesRuleFromQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminRemovesRuleFromQuotaGroup(admin, group, rule)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: exists QuotaGroupRule{group: group, rule: rule}
    ensures: not exists QuotaGroupRule{group: group, rule: rule}
}

-- ---- Holder assignment (site admin) ----------------------------------

-- from: models/quota/group.go:70
rule AdminAddsHolderToQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminAddsHolderToQuotaGroup(admin, group, account)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: not exists QuotaGroupMembership{group: group, account: account}
    ensures: QuotaGroupMembership.created(group: group, account: account, origin: admin_assigned)
    ensures: QuotaGroupsChanged(account: account)
}

-- from: models/quota/group.go:95
rule AdminRemovesHolderFromQuotaGroup {
    when: AdminRemovesHolderFromQuotaGroup(admin, group, account)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    requires: exists QuotaGroupMembership{group: group, account: account}
    ensures: not exists QuotaGroupMembership{group: group, account: account}
    ensures: QuotaGroupsChanged(account: account)
}

-- Replaces the holder's whole explicit group set (an empty set returns the
-- holder to the default groups). All named groups must exist, or nothing changes.
-- from: models/quota/group.go:303
rule AdminSetsHolderQuotaGroups {
    when: AdminSetsHolderQuotaGroups(admin, account, groups)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: config.enabled
    let previous = account.memberships
    ensures:
        for m in previous:
            not exists m
    ensures:
        for g in groups:
            QuotaGroupMembership.created(group: g, account: account, origin: admin_assigned)
    ensures: QuotaGroupsChanged(account: account)
}

-- ---- Login-source sync ------------------------------------------------

-- A group-capable login source (OAuth2 or LDAP) may map the identity
-- provider's groups to quota groups, through the same mapping
-- (AuthSource.quota_group_map). On each sign-in / auto-registration / account
-- link through that source: for every mapped source group the user IS in, the user is added to
-- each mapped quota group (if not already); when the source has "remove
-- unmapped" enabled, the user is removed from each quota group mapped from a
-- source group they are NOT in. Quota groups named by the mapping that do not
-- exist are skipped. For OAuth2 the groups are read from the source's
-- quota-group claim (AuthSource.quota_group_claim_name); for LDAP from the
-- entry's group memberships, as authentication asserts them.
-- from: services/auth/source/source_quota_group_sync.go:15
-- decided (quota 8): every group-capable source syncs quota groups, LDAP
-- included (Forgejo synced OAuth2 only).
-- decided: requests 6 — authentication asserts quota groups in an event of
-- their own, apart from the team-mapping groups.
rule LoginSourceSyncsQuotaGroups {
    when: authentication/ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)
    let account = QuotaAccount{user: user}
    let to_add = quota_groups_mapped_from(source, groups)
    let to_remove = quota_groups_mapped_from_unclaimed(source, groups)
    requires: exists account
    ensures:
        if source.quota_group_map_removal:
            for g in to_remove:
                not exists QuotaGroupMembership{group: g, account: account}
    ensures:
        for g in to_add:
            if not exists QuotaGroupMembership{group: g, account: account}:
                QuotaGroupMembership.created(group: g, account: account, origin: login_source_sync)
    ensures: QuotaGroupsChanged(account: account)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant UniqueRuleName {
    for a in QuotaRules:
        for b in QuotaRules:
            a.name = b.name implies a = b
}

invariant UniqueGroupName {
    for a in QuotaGroups:
        for b in QuotaGroups:
            a.name = b.name implies a = b
}

invariant LimitIsUnlimitedOrNonNegative {
    for r in QuotaRules:
        r.limit >= -1
}

-- decided (follow-up 2): a rule limits bytes or a count, never both.
invariant RuleUnitsNeverMix {
    for r in QuotaRules:
        r.subjects.count = 1 or r.subjects.all(x => x not in {count_repos, count_packages, count_package_versions})
}

invariant AccountHasExactlyOneHolder {
    for a in QuotaAccounts:
        (a.user = null) != (a.organization = null)
}

invariant RuleAtMostOnceInGroup {
    for a in QuotaGroupRules:
        for b in QuotaGroupRules:
            (a.group = b.group and a.rule = b.rule) implies a = b
}

invariant HolderAtMostOnceInGroup {
    for a in QuotaGroupMemberships:
        for b in QuotaGroupMemberships:
            (a.group = b.group and a.account = b.account) implies a = b
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Site administrators are access/SiteAdmin; an organization's owners are
-- organizations/OrgOwner.

-- Any part of the system about to grow someone's storage.
actor StorageConsumer {
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_active = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Site-admin quota management. Present only when quota is enabled.
surface QuotaAdministration {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    exposes:
        for r in QuotaRules:
            r.name when config.enabled
            r.limit when config.enabled
            r.subjects when config.enabled
        for g in QuotaGroups:
            g.name when config.enabled
            for l in g.rule_links:
                l.rule.name when config.enabled
            for m in g.memberships:
                m.account.user.name when config.enabled
                m.account.organization.name when config.enabled
        for a in QuotaAccounts:
            a.usage when config.enabled
            a.memberships when config.enabled

    provides:
        AdminCreatesQuotaRule(admin, name, limit, subjects)
        AdminEditsQuotaRule(admin, rule, new_limit, new_subjects)
        AdminDeletesQuotaRule(admin, rule)
        AdminCreatesQuotaGroup(admin, name, rule_specs)
        AdminDeletesQuotaGroup(admin, group)
        AdminAddsRuleToQuotaGroup(admin, group, rule)
        AdminRemovesRuleFromQuotaGroup(admin, group, rule)
        AdminAddsHolderToQuotaGroup(admin, group, account)
        AdminRemovesHolderFromQuotaGroup(admin, group, account)
        AdminSetsHolderQuotaGroups(admin, account, groups)

    @guidance
        -- API only (no admin web UI). Endpoints:
        --   GET/POST          /admin/quota/rules
        --   GET/PATCH/DELETE  /admin/quota/rules/{rule}
        --   GET/POST          /admin/quota/groups
        --   GET/DELETE        /admin/quota/groups/{group}
        --   PUT/DELETE        /admin/quota/groups/{group}/rules/{rule}
        --   GET               /admin/quota/groups/{group}/users
        --   PUT/DELETE        /admin/quota/groups/{group}/users/{username}
        --   GET               /admin/users/{username}/quota          (usage + effective groups, with names)
        --   POST              /admin/users/{username}/quota/groups   (replace explicit set)
        -- {username} may name an organization.
}

-- A user looking at their own storage.
surface OwnStorageOverview {
    facing viewer: accounts/User
    context account: QuotaAccount where user = viewer

    exposes:
        account.usage.repos_public when config.enabled
        account.usage.repos_private when config.enabled
        account.usage.git_lfs when config.enabled
        account.usage.attachments_issues when config.enabled
        account.usage.attachments_releases when config.enabled
        account.usage.artifacts when config.enabled
        account.usage.packages when config.enabled
        account.usage.wiki when config.enabled
        account.usage.all when config.enabled
        -- decided (follow-up 2): the counts governed by count:* rules
        account.usage.repos_count when config.enabled
        account.usage.packages_count when config.enabled
        account.usage.package_versions_count when config.enabled
        quota_allows(account, subject, null) when config.enabled
        for m in account.memberships:
            for l in m.group.rule_links:
                l.rule.limit when config.enabled
                l.rule.subjects when config.enabled

    @guarantee EffectiveGroupsShown
        -- The overview shows the groups that actually govern the holder: the
        -- explicit ones, else the default groups, else a synthetic "global
        -- quota" with the [quota.default] TOTAL limit on size:all, the
        -- default package limit on size:assets:packages:all and the default
        -- package-version count on count:packages:versions.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/storage_overview (per-subject bars).
        -- API: GET /user/quota (usage + groups; group and rule NAMES are
        --      withheld from non-admins), GET /user/quota/check?subject=…
        --      (boolean quota_allows; unknown subject is refused),
        --      GET /user/quota/{attachments|packages|artifacts} (paginated
        --      list of what consumes storage, largest first).
        -- All absent when quota is disabled.
}

-- An organization owner looking at the organization's storage.
surface OrganizationStorageOverview {
    facing owner: organizations/OrgOwner
    context account: QuotaAccount where organization != null and is_org_owner(organization, owner)

    exposes:
        account.usage.repos_public when config.enabled
        account.usage.repos_private when config.enabled
        account.usage.git_lfs when config.enabled
        account.usage.attachments_issues when config.enabled
        account.usage.attachments_releases when config.enabled
        account.usage.artifacts when config.enabled
        account.usage.packages when config.enabled
        account.usage.wiki when config.enabled
        account.usage.all when config.enabled
        -- decided (follow-up 2): the counts governed by count:* rules
        account.usage.repos_count when config.enabled
        account.usage.packages_count when config.enabled
        account.usage.package_versions_count when config.enabled
        quota_allows(account, subject, null) when config.enabled

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/settings/storage_overview.
        -- API: GET /orgs/{org}/quota, /orgs/{org}/quota/check,
        --      /orgs/{org}/quota/{attachments|packages|artifacts}
        --      (token + organization ownership required).
}

-- The integration boundary every storage-growing operation crosses: the
-- contract each gated operation honours (as quota_allows in its own requires;
-- `incoming` is the operation's size in bytes when known up front, else null),
-- stated here as one stimulus so the gate itself can be exercised. Named apart
-- from the QuotaGate value (one row of the enforcement table).
surface QuotaGateReference {
    facing consumer: StorageConsumer
    context account: QuotaAccount

    provides:
        StorageConsumptionRequested(consumer, account, subject, operation, incoming)

    @guarantee OverQuotaIsRefusedBeforeWork
        -- When the gate refuses, the operation has no effect at all and the
        -- caller is told the quota was exceeded and whose quota it was.

    @guarantee DisabledMeansUngated
        -- With quota disabled every request is admitted.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred quota_allows             -- see: models/quota/quota.go:20 (prose on StorageConsumptionGated; incoming null = size not known up front)
deferred subject_lineage          -- see: models/quota/rule.go:19 (the subject plus its ancestors in the QuotaSubject tree)
deferred quota_groups_mapped_from          -- see: services/auth/source/source_quota_group_sync.go:26 (quota groups mapped from source groups the user is in; unknown group names dropped)
deferred quota_groups_mapped_from_unclaimed -- see: services/auth/source/source_quota_group_sync.go:36 (quota groups mapped from source groups the user is NOT in)
-- Helpers for the gated modules (decided: quota 5 for transfers; the charged
-- party of each QuotaGate names which holder to pass):
--   quota_account_of(holder) = QuotaAccount{user: holder} for a user,
--     QuotaAccount{organization: holder} for an organisation;
--   quota_account_of_owner(repository) = quota_account_of(repository.owner_user
--     or repository.owner_org).
-- A gated module calls quota_allows(quota_account_of_owner(repository), subject,
-- incoming) under its own local name (e.g. code's exceeds_git_quota(r) is
-- not quota_allows(quota_account_of_owner(r), size_repos_all, null)).
deferred quota_account_of         -- see: models/quota/quota.go:20 (the holder's QuotaAccount; one exists for every user and organisation)
deferred quota_account_of_owner   -- see: models/quota/quota.go:20 (quota_account_of the repository's owning user or organisation)
deferred usage_union              -- see: models/quota/rule.go:46 (usage of the union of the subjects: each byte once, so a subject already covered by another listed ancestor adds nothing; decided quota 4. For a count subject it is that count: repos_count, packages_count or package_versions_count; decided follow-up 2)

-- Requests to other modules
-- RESOLVED (accounts): CreateQuotaAccountForNewUser creates the QuotaAccount on accounts/UserAccountCreated(user).
-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.quota_group_claim_name: OAuth2 claim carrying the groups used for quota sync.
-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.quota_group_map: mapping source-group -> set of quota group names (validated JSON).
-- REQUEST authentication/AuthSource.quota_group_map_removal: Boolean, remove memberships for unclaimed mapped groups.
-- REQUEST repositories, code, releases, issues, wiki, pulls, packages, actions: guard each operation listed in the QuotaGate defaults with `requires: quota/quota_allows(<charged account>, <subject>)` (the contract stated by surface QuotaGateReference).
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.git_size, lfs_size; issues/Attachment.size (+ whether it belongs to a release); actions/Artifact.compressed_size and status; packages/PackageBlob.size: the figures QuotaUsage is computed from.
-- REQUEST repositories (mirror scheduler): skip a scheduled pull-mirror sync, without error, while the owner's quota does not allow size_repos_all.
-- REQUEST wiki: measure each wiki's git size (bytes of the wiki repository) and hand it to quota as QuotaUsage.wiki for the repository owner (decided quota 3).
-- REQUEST repositories: WriterRequestsMirrorSync (manual sync, web and API) should check the owner's size:git:all quota rather than the repository-size subject (decided quota 6; gate_mirror_manual).
-- REQUEST issues, releases, packages, actions: pass the incoming size to the quota gate where it is known up front (attachment, release asset, package file, artifact size), so the check is usage + size <= limit (decided quota 2).
-- REQUEST releases, issues, packages: deleting an attachment, release asset or package version must not consult the quota gate (decided quota 7: what can only shrink storage is never refused by quota).
-- REQUEST authentication: emit ExternalGroupsAsserted(user, source, entry.groups) on EVERY LDAP sign-in of an existing account (and on LDAP synchronisation), not only when the account is provisioned, so LDAP quota-group sync works like OAuth2's (decided quota 8). AuthSource.quota_group_map / quota_group_map_removal apply to LDAP sources too.
-- RESOLVED (accounts/authentication): every provisioning path emits accounts/UserAccountCreated, so CreateQuotaAccountForNewUser gives the account its QuotaAccount before the first group sync.
-- REQUEST packages: decided (follow-up 2): before creating a package ask quota_allows(<registry owner>, count_packages, 1) (gate_create_package), and before creating a non-internal version ask quota_allows(<registry owner>, count_package_versions, 1) (gate_create_package_version); QuotaUsage.packages_count / package_versions_count count the owner's non-internal packages / versions - done (quota_allows_new_package / quota_allows_new_version in packages.allium).
-- REQUEST repositories, accounts, organizations: decided (follow-up 2): QuotaUsage.repos_count is the number of repositories the holder owns (accounts/User.num_repos); repositories' within_creation_limit(owner) also requires quota_allows(owner, count_repos, 1) while quota is enabled - done (repositories.allium predicate list).
